      "duration": 2.24
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Put the panda records in order. Find a similarity and a difference.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Young animals can share many features with adults without looking exactly the same.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 5.31
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Tap the stages from youngest to oldest.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.47
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Choose one similarity and one difference.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.52
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a5-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Both have fur, but the adult is larger.",
      "file": "af_bella-a5-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 2.75
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Birds are not the only animals that lay eggs. Match each record to a place.",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.89
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Many kinds of animals lay eggs. Not all egg coverings are hard shells.",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 4.57
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Match each animal’s eggs to the recorded place.",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.92
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Does laying eggs mean an animal must be a bird?",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.97
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a6-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Many kinds of animals lay eggs.",
      "file": "af_bella-a6-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 1.88
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Fix the butterfly life-cycle wheel. Add an event to each stage.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 4.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A caterpillar and an adult butterfly look different, but they are stages of the same kind of animal.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 6.29
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Put the four stages in life-cycle order.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.71
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Match each event to its stage.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 1.81
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A pupa looks still. What can we conclude?",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 2.58
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-step3",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-step3.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a7-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "First comes the egg. Then comes the larva. Next comes the pupa. Finally comes the adult.",
      "file": "af_bella-a7-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 6.25
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A mealworm has a surprising name. Follow the example log to discover its adult stage.",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 6.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A mealworm is a beetle larva. Growing larvae shed their outer covering. This is called molting.",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 6.31
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Read the example log. Arrange earlier to later.",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 3.43
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Which adult does this mealworm become?",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.33
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "What do the butterfly and beetle records share?",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 2.52
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-step3",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-step3.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a8-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A mealworm is a beetle larva.",
      "file": "af_bella-a8-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 2.07
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Match body features to their jobs. Choose an observation that supports your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 5.61
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Traits can help animals move, find food, or stay safe. Use observations to explain the connection.",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 7.34
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Connect each feature to the job it helps with.",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.73
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Which observation supports “claws help it dig”?",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 3.03
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a9-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Its claws help it dig in the soil.",
      "file": "af_bella-a9-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 2.05
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Predict which background makes the green insect harder to notice. Change only the background, then compare.",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 6.91
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Similar colors can make an animal harder to notice. This is a picture model, not a test of every real predator.",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 7.38
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Predict first. Then view both backgrounds.",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.75
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "What stayed the same in our comparison?",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.15
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Which conclusion fits this model?",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 2.07
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-step3",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-step3.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a10-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "In this model, the green background makes the green insect harder to notice.",
      "file": "af_bella-a10-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 4.78
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Find all rabbits in Area A. Use both the species and the study area to make your group.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 5.85
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A population includes the same species in an area. Individuals share traits but need not look exactly the same.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 7.7
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Select all rabbits in Area A, and no other animals.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 3.39
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Choose two statements supported by the rabbit records.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.99
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build your explanation.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-step2.mp3",
      "duration": 1.45
    },
    {
      "id": "a11-sentence",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "These rabbits are the same species in one study area.",
      "file": "af_bella-a11-sentence.mp3",
      "duration": 3.33
    },
    {
      "id": "a12-intro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build a frog display. Combine life-cycle records and body clues to correct a mistaken label.",
      "file": "af_bella-a12-intro.mp3",
      "duration": 6.19
    },
    {
      "id": "a12-fact",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "A tadpole is a young amphibian. Follow its life cycle and use evidence, not just its home, to explain its group.",
      "file": "af_bella-a12-fact.mp3",
      "duration": 7.91
    },
    {
      "id": "a12-step0",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Build the frog life-cycle display.",
      "file": "af_bella-a12-step0.mp3",
      "duration": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "a12-step1",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Add the body clues to the correct stages.",
      "file": "af_bella-a12-step1.mp3",
      "duration": 2.47
    },
    {
      "id": "a12-step2",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "text": "Fix this label: “A tadpole is a fish because it lives in water.”",
      "file": "af_bella-a12-step2.mp3",
